<title>USA: MascoTech buys German forging company.</title>
<headline>MascoTech buys German forging company.</headline>
<dateline>TAYLOR, Mich. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>MascoTech Inc said Tuesday it acquired  Neumeyer Flieapressen GmbH, a manufacturer of cold-forged components for the automotive original equipment market, from  Hoogovens Group, a steel company based in The Netherlands.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. Based in Nuremberg, Germany, Neumeyer will operate as a subsidiary of Holzer &amp; Company GmbH, MascoTech's European forging operation.</p>
<p>In addition to the Nuremberg manufacturing facility, Neumeyer also operates a manufacturing facility in Oslavany, Czech Republic. The company currently employs approximately 300 people.</p>
</text>
